{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c70f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a895-af1e-7030-b7a0-b39b63843e96"},"sequence":482,"recorded_at":1780531400000959,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332"},"call_id":"call_01a0a896d43870c39b72f7b3e801adc4","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/outputs/RunnerControl/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260916-13diw4/TASK-260916-13diw4_review-verdict-rev2.md`.\n1|# Verdict: changes_requested\n2|\n3|Task: TASK-260916-13diw4\n4|Change Request: CR-TASK-260916-13diw4-2, revision 2\n5|Candidate: 0973915f402f3e526683c3bb12d8d908b714d7c4\n6|Route: to-dev\n7|repeat-of: revision 1 / F5 (foreign-runner non-disruption class; see R2-F2). Other per-finding values below.\n8|\n9|## Evidence and scope\n10|\n11|AC evidence checked before code: producer maps **8 of 8 AC rows driven** to named production-entry tests. This is a driving-test ratio, not satisfaction. Counterexamples below invalidate claimed registration/access behavior (rows 1–4 and 6); safe failure and no-secret evidence is bounded by exercised paths. The mutant table includes narrowing mutants, not only deletions. M9 is explicitly reported as a survivor with M9b exercising the load-bearing call site.\n12|\n13|Read complete attached rev2 validation log: 110 Core tests and four metadata tests exit 0, with final command and shard summary present. Accepted as producer baseline evidence, not independently replayed wholesale. Build/lint prose was not independently rerun or accepted as proof of these behaviors.\n14|\n15|Exported the exact candidate with git archive to `/tmp/rc-review-13diw4-r2`. Appended only review test code to the disposable copy. Production files were unchanged. Independently ran:\n16|\n17|- `swift test --package-path /tmp/rc-review-13diw4-r2/Packages/RunnerControlCore --filter reviewR2`: **exit 1; six tests, all six failed, 12 assertions**. Full log and appended test source attached.\n18|- Seven focused regression controls covering rev1 checksum, HTTP 204, public-group create/patch, name-only group takeover refusal, implicit runner replacement refusal, and post-config token deletion: **exit 0; seven passed**. Full log attached.\n19|\n20|All 19 reviewed workspace paths still byte-match the immutable candidate. No production runner, live GitHub mutation, UI test, or product-code edit occurred. `task-board spawn goal` reports this run is not goal-bound.\n21|\n22|## Required changes\n23|\n24|### R2-F1 — P1: list requests encode the query into the path\n25|\n26|`GitHubRunnerAPIClient.swift:34,191,216` passes `...?per_page=100` to `appendingPathComponent`. Actual outbound artifacts are `.../runners%3Fper_page=100` and `.../runner-groups%3Fper_page=100`, with nil URL query. These do not address GitHub's documented list routes. This breaks group resolution and the pre-registration list read. The queue transport accepts arbitrary URLs and hides it.\n27|\n28|Production test: `reviewR2ListURLsUseQueryNotEncodedPath` drives Flow.resolveGroup and Flow.applyLabels, asserting the emitted request URL components; four assertions fail. Shape: capability claim that does not reproduce / green suite around a permissive fake. Build paths and query items separately; make controlled transports assert method/path/query and test both org/repo list paths. repeat-of: none.\n29|\n30|### R2-F2 — P1: a remote name match authorizes writes to another runner\n31|\n32|`RunnerRegistration+Flow.swift:430–435,540–561` resolves identity by name and treats it as authority for label PUTs. `reviewR2NameOnlyMustNotAuthorizeLabelMutation` drives beginDraft then applyLabels with no local installation or registration: a same-name remote runner 77 is mutated. `reviewR2MismatchedLocalAgentMustNotBecomeRemoteIdentity` registers fixture local agent 4242, returns remote same-name 77, then proves labels are written to 77. The producer end-to-end test explicitly accepts this mismatch. The UI's button disablement does not repair the registered mismatch path.\n33|\n34|Shape: absent ownership evidence treated as satisfied; bypass around the non-disruption boundary. Bind remote identity to verified local .runner server/scope/agentId, not name; refuse missing, malformed, mismatched, or ambiguous identity before writes. Commit these regressions and a narrowing mutant admitting exactly one mismatched agent ID, including retry/resume. This is rework in this leaf, not a separate harness task.\n35|\n36|repeat-of: revision 1 / F5, same foreign-runner non-disruption class; the old unconditional --replace mechanism is fixed, but the same protected boundary is bypassed through labels. Also explicitly anticipated by rev1's unnumbered identity bound.\n37|\n38|### R2-F3 — P1: editing scope retains the old installation and runner ID\n39|\n40|`RunnerRegistration+Flow.swift:124–130` clears only group/asset on scope change. `installPath`, runnerID and step progress remain. Container field callbacks dispatch updateDraft and Apply Labels remains enabled while the old runnerID is present. `reviewR2ChangedScopeMustNotReuseRegistrationOrRemoteID` registers org acme agent 4242, edits to repo octo/app and a different install directory, then observes PUT `/repos/octo/app/actions/runners/4242/labels` without registering that installation. Other later steps likewise retain the old path.\n41|\n42|Shape: bypass path through edit/retry; stale evidence reused under a changed identity. Bind operation progress and consent to immutable server/scope/path/name/group identity, or safely invalidate dependent progress on changes. Do not describe this as acceptable 'current draft' behavior: it directs writes using a different registration's evidence. Add scope/path/group edits during and after work plus retry tests and a narrowing mutant. repeat-of: none (explicitly flagged in rev1 as an unnumbered rework bound).\n43|\n44|### R2-F4 — P1: partial repository lists are reported as complete confirmation\n45|\n46|`GitHubRunnerAPIClient.swift:321–322` ignores pagination; Flow.applyRepositoryAccess replaces the draft's selected IDs with the returned first page and emits success. `reviewR2RepositoryConfirmationMustFollowPagination` returns a valid first page with total_count and a next Link, then a second page: the flow emits `[9]` instead of `[9,10]` and never requests page 2. A later apply can consequently delete access omitted from the first page. Adding per_page=100 to other endpoints does not implement complete listing.\n47|\n48|Shape: partial read presented as complete evidence. Follow pagination for repository, runner and group lists; preserve failure/unknown on any failed page and compare complete confirmed IDs to requested IDs. Add multipage/second-page-failure production tests and a narrowing mutant skipping only later pages. repeat-of: none (explicitly flagged in rev1 as an unnumbered rework bound).\n49|\n50|### R2-F5 — P2: service setup declares registration complete without registration\n51|\n52|`RunnerRegistration+Flow.swift:443–456` requires only draft/installPath. WizardSteps exposes Setup Service even when registration was skipped/failed. `reviewR2ServiceCannotClaimDoneBeforeRegistration` downloads the package, skips registration, then receives serviceReady and a written manual-service.plist. The reducer maps serviceReady to phase done and the page says the runner is registered.\n53|\n54|Shape: absent evidence treated as satisfied. Require verified configured local identity for this operation before service creation/completion; reflect prerequisite state in UI. Add skipped/failed/corrupt-registration tests and a narrowing mutant. repeat-of: none.\n55|\n56|## API contract correction and remaining bounds\n57|\n58|GitHub's rendered download examples omit checksum, but its official OpenAPI runner-application schema DOES define optional `sha256_checksum`. Inspected the actual schema via a read-only download; required fields are os, architecture, download_url and filename. Therefore the producer is correct that the field exists in the schema. Fail-closed missing-checksum behavior is now tested and passes; no claim is made here about actual checksum availability for a live authenticated response. That remains the separate smoke task's bound, not an inferred absence.\n59|\n60|Sources: https://github.com/github/rest-api-description/blob/main/descriptions/api.github.com/api.github.com.json ; https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/self-hosted-runners ; https://docs.github.com/en/rest/actions/self-hosted-runner-groups\n61|\n62|Container → Flow → actor services → reducer wiring fits the existing architecture. The five demonstrated defects require implementation rework, not a human decision or external blocker. Preserve the seven now-green controls while adding regressions above.\n63|\n64|Logbook: no logbook executable, connector, or repository logbook was available. Findings are persisted in this artifact and task notes rather than creating product files.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c711","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a895-af1e-7030-b7a0-b39b63843e96"},"sequence":483,"recorded_at":1780531400000961,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332"},"call_id":"call_01a0a896d5be76f58e5359934dde1cdb","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/outputs/RunnerControl/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260916-13diw4/TASK-260916-13diw4_review-attacks-rev2.swift`.\n1|\n2|// Reviewer attacks; appended only to git-archived rev2 in /tmp.\n3|@Test func reviewR2ListURLsUseQueryNotEncodedPath() async throws {\n4|    let transport = TestTransport([\n5|        groupsListPayload([]),\n6|        jsonResponse(groupPayload(id: 5, name: \"RunnerControl-Mac\", visibility: \"selected\", allowsPublic: true), status: 201),\n7|        jsonResponse([\"repositories\": []]),\n8|        runnersListPayload([])\n9|    ])\n10|    let h = await registrationHarness(transport: transport)\n11|    defer { try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: h.home) }\n12|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.beginDraft(orgDraft()))\n13|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.resolveGroup)\n14|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.applyLabels([\"gpu\"]))\n15|    let requests = await transport.requests\n16|    let lists = requests.filter { $0.url.absoluteString.contains(\"per_page\") }\n17|    #expect(lists.count == 2)\n18|    for request in lists {\n19|        #expect(!request.url.absoluteString.contains(\"%3F\"))\n20|        #expect(URLComponents(url: request.url, resolvingAgainstBaseURL: false)?.queryItems?.contains(URLQueryItem(name: \"per_page\", value: \"100\")) == true)\n21|    }\n22|}\n23|\n24|@Test func reviewR2NameOnlyMustNotAuthorizeLabelMutation() async throws {\n25|    let transport = TestTransport([\n26|        runnersListPayload([[\"id\": 77, \"name\": \"macbook-test\", \"labels\": []]]),\n27|        jsonResponse([\"labels\": [[\"name\": \"gpu\"]]])\n28|    ])\n29|    let h = await registrationHarness(transport: transport)\n30|    defer { try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: h.home) }\n31|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.beginDraft(orgDraft()))\n32|    // No install, no local agent ID, no successful registration; foreign name match only.\n33|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.applyLabels([\"gpu\"]))\n34|    #expect(await transport.requests.filter { $0.method == \"PUT\" }.isEmpty)\n35|    #expect(!registrationActions(h.logger).contains { if case .labelsApplied = $0 { true } else { false } })\n36|}\n37|\n38|@Test func reviewR2ChangedScopeMustNotReuseRegistrationOrRemoteID() async throws {\n39|    let package = try await FixturePackage.make(withRealConfigScript: false)\n40|    let executor = SplitExecutor()\n41|    let transport = TestTransport([\n42|        downloadsArrayPayload(downloadAssets(checksum: package.sha256ViaSystem)),\n43|        runnersListPayload([]),\n44|        jsonResponse([\"token\": \"REVIEW-TOKEN\", \"expires_at\": \"2030-01-01T00:00:00Z\"], status: 201),\n45|        runnersListPayload([[\"id\": 4242, \"name\": \"macbook-test\", \"labels\": []]]),\n46|        jsonResponse([\"labels\": [[\"name\": \"gpu\"]]])\n47|    ])\n48|    let h = await registrationHarness(transport: transport, downloader: fixtureDownloader(package.bytes), executor: executor)\n49|    defer { try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: h.home) }\n50|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.beginDraft(orgDraft()))\n51|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.downloadAndInstall)\n52|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.registerRunner)\n53|    // Actual Container dispatches updateDraft for edits and leaves Apply Labels enabled.\n54|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.updateDraft(repoDraft(dir: \"different-install\")))\n55|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.applyLabels([\"gpu\"]))\n56|    let foreignWrites = await transport.requests.filter { $0.method == \"PUT\" && $0.url.path.contains(\"/repos/octo/app/actions/runners/4242/labels\") }\n57|    #expect(foreignWrites.isEmpty)\n58|}\n59|\n60|@Test func reviewR2MismatchedLocalAgentMustNotBecomeRemoteIdentity() async throws {\n61|    let package = try await FixturePackage.make(withRealConfigScript: false)\n62|    let transport = TestTransport([\n63|        downloadsArrayPayload(downloadAssets(checksum: package.sha256ViaSystem)),\n64|        runnersListPayload([]),\n65|        jsonResponse([\"token\": \"REVIEW-TOKEN\", \"expires_at\": \"2030-01-01T00:00:00Z\"], status: 201),\n66|        runnersListPayload([[\"id\": 77, \"name\": \"macbook-test\", \"labels\": []]]),\n67|        jsonResponse([\"labels\": [[\"name\": \"gpu\"]]])\n68|    ])\n69|    let h = await registrationHarness(transport: transport, downloader: fixtureDownloader(package.bytes), executor: SplitExecutor())\n70|    defer { try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: h.home) }\n71|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.beginDraft(orgDraft()))\n72|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.downloadAndInstall)\n73|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.registerRunner)\n74|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.applyLabels([\"gpu\"]))\n75|    #expect(await h.installer.readAgentID(directory: h.installRoot.appendingPathComponent(\"macbook-test\")) == 4242)\n76|    #expect(await transport.requests.filter { $0.method == \"PUT\" && $0.url.path.contains(\"/77/labels\") }.isEmpty)\n77|}\n78|\n79|@Test func reviewR2ServiceCannotClaimDoneBeforeRegistration() async throws {\n80|    let package = try await FixturePackage.make(withRealConfigScript: false)\n81|    let transport = TestTransport([downloadsArrayPayload(downloadAssets(checksum: package.sha256ViaSystem))])\n82|    let h = await registrationHarness(transport: transport, downloader: fixtureDownloader(package.bytes), executor: SplitExecutor())\n83|    defer { try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: h.home) }\n84|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.beginDraft(orgDraft()))\n85|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.downloadAndInstall)\n86|    // Wizard exposes this step while connected even when registration was skipped/failed.\n87|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.setupService)\n88|    #expect(!registrationActions(h.logger).contains { if case .serviceReady = $0 { true } else { false } })\n89|    #expect(!FileManager.default.fileExists(atPath: h.installRoot.appendingPathComponent(\"macbook-test/manual-service.plist\").path))\n90|}\n91|\n92|@Test func reviewR2RepositoryConfirmationMustFollowPagination() async throws {\n93|    let transport = TestTransport([\n94|        groupsListPayload([groupPayload(id: 5, name: \"RunnerControl-Mac\", visibility: \"selected\", allowsPublic: true)]),\n95|        jsonResponse([\"repositories\": [[\"id\": 9]]]),\n96|        GitHubHTTPResponse(status: 204, body: Data()),\n97|        GitHubHTTPResponse(status: 200, headers: [\"Link\": \"<https://api.github.com/orgs/acme/actions/runner-groups/5/repositories?page=2>; rel=\\\"next\\\"\"], body: try JSONSerialization.data(withJSONObject: [\"total_count\": 2, \"repositories\": [[\"id\": 9]]])),\n98|        jsonResponse([\"total_count\": 2, \"repositories\": [[\"id\": 10]]])\n99|    ])\n100|    let h = await registrationHarness(transport: transport)\n101|    defer { try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: h.home) }\n102|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.beginDraft(orgDraft(allowTakeover: true)))\n103|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.resolveGroup)\n104|    _ = await h.flow.apply(RunnerRegistration.Effect.applyRepositoryAccess(groupID: 5, repositories: [9,10]))\n105|    let confirmed = registrationActions(h.logger).compactMap { a -> [Int64]? in\n106|        if case .repositoryAccessApplied(let ids) = a { ids } else { nil }\n107|    }\n108|    #expect(confirmed.last.map(Set.init) == Set<Int64>([9,10]))\n109|    #expect(await transport.requests.contains { $0.url.query?.contains(\"page=2\") == true })\n110|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c713","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a895-af1e-7030-b7a0-b39b63843e96"},"sequence":484,"recorded_at":1780531400000963,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332"},"call_id":"call_01a0a896d79475c5b1f322e8ebf6256d","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Documents/Codex/2026-09-15/new-chat-4/outputs/RunnerControl/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260916-13diw4/TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260916-13diw4: register-mac-and-repository-access — developer outcome\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review (board `to-review`, uncommitted candidate in story worktree).\n4|\n5|## What was delivered\n6|\n7|New-runner wizard through the GitHub API, wired through the existing Relux\n8|stack (Page → Container → Effect/Flow → actor services → Action/Reducer →\n9|State). The worktree already contained a staged wizard implementation (99\n10|green tests); this run kept that architecture and closed the four review-focus\n11|gaps from `review-focus-live-and-scope.md` plus all six demonstrated failures\n12|(F1–F6) from the prior Astra review rev1 (`changes_requested`,\n13|`repeat-of: none`):\n14|\n15|1. **`allows_public_repositories`** — dedicated groups now opt in on create\n16|   (`POST …/runner-groups` sends `allows_public_repositories: true`) and an\n17|   adopted owned group that denies public repos is patched\n18|   (`PATCH …/runner-groups/{id}`). Without this GitHub's default (`false`)\n19|   silently drops every selected public repo even though `visibility:\n20|   selected` lists it. `RunnerGroup` now carries the flag and the UI shows it.\n21|2. **Unconditional `config --replace`** — removed. `ConfigInvocation` omits\n22|   `--replace` unless `Draft.allowReplace` (explicit UI toggle) is set, and\n23|   `Flow.registerRunner` refuses a remote name match *before minting any\n24|   registration token* (`remoteNameTaken`), so a duplicate name can never\n25|   silently steal another Mac's registration. New errors, gates, tests.\n26|3. **Group-name reuse ownership** — a name match alone no longer authorizes\n27|   adoption. `RunnerInstallerService` keeps an ownership table at\n28|   `<installRoot>/.runnercontrol-groups.json` (`org ␀ name → groupID`);\n29|   `Flow.resolveGroup` requires either a matching ownership entry or explicit\n30|   `Draft.allowGroupTakeover` (UI toggle), else `groupNameTaken`. Creation and\n31|   takeover record ownership so retries on this Mac reuse without re-confirming.\n32|4. **Checksum availability (F1)** — GitHub's downloads endpoint documents\n33|   `sha256_checksum`, so the installer now fails closed: a missing/empty\n34|   checksum throws `integrityMismatch` instead of skipping verification.\n35|5. **HTTP 204 rejected (F2)** — `PUT …/runner-groups/{id}/repositories`\n36|   answers `204 No Content` in production, but the client accepted only\n37|   200/201, failing every production repo-access update. `send()` now accepts\n38|   204; only the two body-ignoring PUTs can legally return it.\n39|6. **Post-config token retention (F6)** — when the follow-up runner-ID lookup\n40|   failed after a successful `config.sh`, the single-use registration token\n41|   stayed in Keychain. The token is now deleted immediately after config\n42|   succeeds (it is consumed at that point), before any follow-up API call.\n43|\n44|Supporting changes: `fetchRunners`/`fetchGroups` use `per_page=100`; new\n45|`updateGroupAllowsPublic` client call; `runConfig` threads the explicit\n46|`replace` flag; Container/Page wire the two new consent toggles.\n47|\n48|## AC coverage — 8 of 8 rows driven through production entry points\n49|\n50|| # | AC row | Named committed test(s) | Production call site |\n51||---|--------|-------------------------|----------------------|\n52|| 1 | Org registration without terminal | `orgWizardEndToEndDeletesTokenAndLeaksNothing` | `RunnerRegistration.Flow.apply` (.beginDraft/.resolveGroup/.downloadAndInstall/.registerRunner/.setupService) |\n53|| 2 | Repo registration without terminal | `repoWizardOmitsRunnerGroup` | same Flow effects; asserts no `runner-groups` traffic, no `--runnergroup` argv |\n54|| 3 | Selected repos are applied | `orgResolveGroupCreatesWithSelectedRepos`, `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs` | `GitHubRunnerAPIClient.createGroup` / `setGroupRepositories` + `fetchGroupRepositories` confirm |\n55|| 4 | Repo access and labels changeable | `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs` ([9]→[9,10]), `labelsApplyRequiresRealRunnerIDThenPuts` | `Flow.apply(.applyRepositoryAccess/.applyLabels)` → `setGroupRepositories` / `setRunnerLabels` with real IDs |\n56|| 5 | Failed ops avoid orphans | `failedConfigDeletesTokenAndReportsScrubbedError`, `registerIsIdempotentAcrossRetries` | `Flow.registerRunner` (token deleted on config failure; single mint + single config across retries) |\n57|| 6 | Repeated ops avoid duplicates | `registerIsIdempotentAcrossRetries`, `retryResumesFailedDownloadWithoutDuplicates`, `remoteDuplicateWithoutReplaceIsRefusedBeforeToken`, `existingRegistrationBlocksFreshInstall` | `Flow.registerRunner` resume path + `rejectRemoteDuplicate` gate; installer markers |\n58|| 7 | No secret leakage | `orgWizardEndToEndDeletesTokenAndLeaksNothing`, `runConfigScrubsTokenFromFailure`, `failedConfigDeletesTokenAndReportsScrubbedError` | token reaches only config.sh argv in memory; absent from actions/URLs/headers/bodies; scrubbed from errors; deleted after use |\n59|| 8 | Tests exercise actual entry points | all Flow tests above + `setupServiceWritesManualPlistFoundByDiscovery`, `runConfigExecutesRealScript` | `Flow.apply`, `RunnerInstallerService.downloadAndInstall/runConfig/setupService`, cross-checked by `RunnerDiscovery.installed` and a real shell `config.sh` |\n60|\n61|Negative/refusal coverage (all fail when the gate admits what it must reject):\n62|`beginDraftRefusesSpacesBeforeAnyNetwork`, `installerRefusesSpacesWithoutDownloading`,\n63|`beginDraftRequiresNameAndLabels`, `unauthenticatedWizardFailsClosedWithoutNetwork`,\n64|`prepareDownloadRefusesSubstituteArch`, `downloadRefusesTamperedBytes`,\n65|`downloadRefusesMalformedChecksum`, `downloadRefusesMissingChecksum`,\n66|`existingRegistrationBlocksFreshInstall`, `existingGroupNameWithoutTakeoverIsRefused`,\n67|`repoScopeRefusesGroupResolution`, `repoAccessWithoutExplicitScopeIsRefused`,\n68|`repoAccessToForeignGroupIsRefused`, `remoteDuplicateWithoutReplaceIsRefusedBeforeToken`,\n69|`recoverPartialInstallRefusesWorkingRunner`, `runConfigScrubsTokenFromFailure`,\n70|`permissionErrorRetainedAcrossEditsUntilRetrySucceeds`,\n71|`forbiddenGroupCreateNamesRequiredPermission`, plus the refusal half of\n72|`labelsApplyRequiresRealRunnerIDThenPuts`.\n73|\n74|## Narrowing-mutant evidence\n75|\n76|Each mutant keeps the gate present and weakens it to admit exactly one member\n77|of the rejected class. All runs are `swift test --package-path\n78|Packages/RunnerControlCore --filter <test>`; files verified pristine (`cmp`)\n79|after each revert.\n80|\n81|| Mutant | Narrows the gate to admit | Named failing test | Result |\n82||--------|---------------------------|--------------------|--------|\n83|| M1: `contains(\" \")` → `contains(\"  \")` on install dir | single-space `\"bad dir\"` | `beginDraftRefusesSpacesBeforeAnyNetwork` | KILLED, exit 1 (2 issues; the `workFolder` case still passes) |\n84|| M2: `selectDownload` matches OS only | osx/x64 asset for an arm64 Mac | `prepareDownloadRefusesSubstituteArch` | KILLED, exit 1 |\n85|| M3: `authorizeGroupMutation` skips consent when IDs match | unconfirmed write to resolved group 5 | `repoAccessWithoutExplicitScopeIsRefused` | KILLED, exit 1 (mutant reached network: request count grew) |\n86|| M4: `authorizeGroupMutation` additionally admits `targetGroupID == 1` | write to foreign group 1 | `repoAccessToForeignGroupIsRefused` | KILLED, exit 1 (mutant reached network) |\n87|| M5: `requireOrganizationScope` admits `repository(owner: \"octo\", …)` | `octo/app` repo scope | `repoScopeRefusesGroupResolution` | KILLED, exit 1 |\n88|| M6: `authorizeGroupTakeover` admits `existingID == 5` | name-alone adoption of group 5 | `existingGroupNameWithoutTakeoverIsRefused` | KILLED, exit 1 (3 issues incl. ownership file written) |\n89|| M7: `rejectRemoteDuplicate` admits name `\"macbook-test\"` | duplicate `macbook-test` | `remoteDuplicateWithoutReplaceIsRefusedBeforeToken` | KILLED, exit 1 (mutant minted a `registration-token` POST) |\n90|| M8: checksum guard restored to skip-when-missing | nil-checksum package | `downloadRefusesMissingChecksum` | KILLED, exit 1 (mutant installed `run.sh`) |\n91|| M9: `createGroup` default `allowsPublicRepositories` true→false | — | `orgResolveGroupCreatesWithSelectedRepos` | SURVIVED, exit 0 — bound: the default is not load-bearing; Flow passes `true` explicitly (see M9b) |\n92|| M9b: Flow call site passes `allowsPublicRepositories: false` | group created denying public repos | `orgResolveGroupCreatesWithSelectedRepos` | KILLED, exit 1 (body `false`, expected `true`) |\n93|| M10: `ConfigInvocation` adds `--replace` when `runnerGroup != nil` | unconsented `--replace` on org runs | `runConfigOmitsReplaceByDefault` | KILLED, exit 1 (argv ended in `--replace`) |\n94|| M11 (F2): `send()` accepts only 200/201 | production 204 repos-PUT fails | `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs` (204 fixture) | KILLED, exit 1 (no IDs applied) |\n95|| M12 (F6): token deleted only after follow-up succeeds | token retained on post-config API failure | `postConfigAPIFailureDeletesTokenAndReportsError` | KILLED, exit 1 (token still stored) |\n96|\n97|The source-text-token mutant rule does not apply: none of these gates inspect\n98|source text (no searched-for token to preserve while changing behavior).\n99|\n100|## Verification commands (real exit codes)\n101|\n102|- `swift test --package-path Packages/RunnerControlCore` (CI gate): **exit 0,\n103|  110 tests passed** (99 baseline + 11 new: 10 gap tests + F6 regression; F2\n104|  reuses `repoAccessAppliesAndConfirmsRealIDs` with a production-faithful 204\n105|  fixture).\n106|- `xcodebuild -workspace RunnerControl.xcworkspace -scheme RunnerControlCore\n107|  -destination 'platform=macOS' test`: **exit 0, 109 passed** (same suite via\n108|  Xcode, run before the F2/F6 additions; final 110-count proven by the CI\n109|  gate above).\n110|- `xcodebuild -workspace RunnerControl.xcworkspace -scheme RunnerControl\n111|  -destination 'platform=macOS' build`: **BUILD SUCCEEDED** (exit 0) with one\n112|  pre-existing Swift 6 Sendable warning at\n113|  `RunnerRegistrationPage.swift:157` (scope Picker binding, untouched line\n114|  from staged code).\n115|- No repo-configured lint gate (no SwiftLint config in repo; CI runs only the\n116|  two test jobs above). No new compiler warnings introduced.\n117|- Generator inputs untouched: `ios-app-manager.json`, `Project.swift`,\n118|  `Workspace.swift` unmodified (verified via `git status`).\n119|\n120|## Files changed (all UNCOMMITTED in story worktree, as required)\n121|\n122|- `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Sources/RunnerRegistration+Models.swift` —\n123|  `Draft.allowGroupTakeover/allowReplace`, `RunnerGroup.allowsPublicRepositories`,\n124|  `groupNameTaken`/`remoteNameTaken` errors.\n125|- `…/RunnerRegistration+Gates.swift` — `authorizeGroupTakeover`,\n126|  `rejectRemoteDuplicate`, `ConfigSpec.replace`, conditional `--replace`.\n127|- `…/GitHubRunnerAPIClient.swift` — `allows_public_repositories` decode/encode,\n128|  `updateGroupAllowsPublic`, `per_page=100` on runners/groups lists.\n129|- `…/RunnerInstallerService.swift` — fail-closed checksum, `runConfig`\n130|  replace threading, group-ownership store.\n131|- `…/RunnerRegistration+Flow.swift` — ownership-checked resolve,\n132|  allows-public ensure, pre-token duplicate guard.\n133|- `Targets/RunnerControl/Sources/RunnerRegistrationContainer.swift`,\n134|  `RunnerRegistrationPage.swift` — two consent toggles, public-repos display.\n135|- `Packages/RunnerControlCore/Tests/RunnerRegistrationTests.swift` — 10 new\n136|  tests + updated transports/fixtures for the stricter behavior.\n137|\n138|## Stated bounds (unknowns, not guesses)\n139|\n140|- Duplicate-name pre-check reads the first runners page (`per_page=100`); a\n141|  duplicate beyond it is still safe because `config.sh` omits `--replace`\n142|  without consent and fails instead of stealing.\n143|- Remote runner IDs are resolved by name match (`resolveRemoteRunnerID`):\n144|  inherent to the classic registration-token flow, which returns no ID;\n145|  the pre-check + fail-closed config bound the collision window but a\n146|  same-name runner created concurrently on another Mac resolves ambiguously.\n147|- Retry runs the *current* draft, not a snapshot: a draft edit between\n148|  failure and retry changes what the retried step executes (review's\n149|  \"mutable draft/progress identity\" bound, kept as designed behavior).\n150|- Ownership table is per-Mac (`~/Library/GitHubActions/.runnercontrol-groups.json`):\n151|  it distinguishes this Mac's groups from same-name groups on other Macs, but\n152|  two local users on one Mac do not share it (same as installs themselves).\n153|- No live-GitHub verification in this run: real OAuth/registration smoke is a\n154|  separate delivery task per the brief; transport is covered by fakes and the\n155|  filesystem by temp-root fixtures with a real `tar`/`shasum`/`config.sh`.\n156|- The wizard never touches existing production runners: all filesystem writes\n157|  stay under the chosen new install dir + ownership file; no stop, re-register,\n158|  or service bootstrap of existing runners (setup writes the plist only and\n159|  never bootstraps it).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
