{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e151","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0a895-af1e-7030-b7a0-b39b63843e96"},"sequence":3843,"recorded_at":1780531400007681,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"a6dbad5b-a9c9-418a-a77b-cbe6123a6332"},"terminal":"completed","text":"All five revision-2 findings are fixed and handed off to review.\n\nWhat changed: list URLs now use real `per_page` query items instead of encoded `%3F` paths, and all three list endpoints follow `Link` pagination to completion. Label writes, registration, and service setup require the verified local `.runner` identity (configured marker + agent ID + name + scope) and bind the remote runner by ID — a same-name foreign runner fails instead of being adopted or mutated. Draft edits invalidate dependent progress in both Flow and reducer (scope/install/name/group matrices, `.done` demotion), repo-access confirmation must exactly equal the request, and Setup Service is gated on completed registration in code and UI.\n\nEvidence: 132 Core tests green via the CI gate (exit 0, 110 + 22 new R2 regressions), metadata tests 4/4, app `BUILD SUCCEEDED` with only pre-existing warnings. Narrowing mutants M13–M20 killed (each reverted pristine), M1–M8/M9b/M10–M12 re-killed; M9 survives with its stated bound (default not load-bearing, M9b kills the call site). AC coverage 8 of 8 rows driven through production entry points, documented in `TASK-260916-13diw4_outcome_v3.md`.\n\nThe candidate is uncommitted in the story worktree, no scaffold files touched, no production runners disturbed. Ready for review.","reason":null}}
